  "song_id": "3PhoLpVuITZKcymswpck5b::abide-with-me",
  "title": "Abide with me",
  "artist": "Elton John",
  "genre": "unknown",
  "original_lyrics": "[verse]\n1. -bide with me, fast falls the eventide.\nThe darkness deepens, Lord, with me -bide.\nWhen other helpers fail, and comforts flee,\nhelp of the helpless, oh, - bide with me!\n2. I need thy presence every passing hour!\nWhat but Thy grace can foil the tempter's pow'r?\nWho like Thyself my guide and stay can be?\nThrough cloud and sunshine, oh, - bide with me !\n3. Swift to it's close ebbs out life's little day.\nEarth's joys grow dim, it's glories pass -way.\n\n[chorus]\nO Thou who changest not, - bide with me !\n4. Not brief glance I beg, passing word.\n\n[bridge]\nFamiliar, condescending, patient, free.\n\n[chorus]\n5. Come not in terror, as the King of kings,\n\n[bridge]\nTears for all woes, heart for every plea.\n\n[chorus]\n6. Thou on my head in every youth didst smile.\nAnd though rebellious and perverse meanwhile,\nThou hast not left me, oft as I left Thee.\nOn to the close, O Lord, - bide with me.\n7. I fear no foe, with Thee at hand to bless.\nIlls have no weight, and tears no bitterness.\nWhere is death's sting? Where, grave, thy victory?\nI triumph still, if thou - bide with me!\n8. Hold thou thy cross be-fore my closing eyes.\nShine through the gloom, and point me to the skies.\nHeav'n's morning breaks, and earth's vain shadows flee.",
